No loopd source code is included in loopmark. What was taken is the discovery
work: which DOM structures Microsoft Loop actually uses. Specifically, the
following facts recorded in `src/selectors.ts` were learned from reading
`plugins/loopd-loop-export/loopd.js`:

  - Loop's editor is internally named "Scriptor" and prefixes its class names
    accordingly (scriptor-pageContainer, scriptor-paragraph, and so on).
  - The ordered list of page content container selectors.
  - Loop renders links as <span role="link"> with the destination in the
    `title` attribute, not as <a href>.
  - Loop associates list items with their list via `aria-owns`, and renders a
    duplicate `aria-hidden` copy of those items.
  - The class names for headings, callouts, code blocks, tasks, dividers,
    table rows and cells, and the collapse-button container.
  - The page title selectors, including [data-automation-type="Title"].

loopmark's architecture is deliberately different: loopd is a DevTools console
script that loads the remark ecosystem from esm.sh at runtime. loopmark makes
zero network requests and ships a hand-written converter with no runtime
dependencies. See SECURITY.md for why that distinction is the whole point.

